<title>SRI LANKA: Sri Lanka Kotagala dips on profit-taking.</title>
<headline>Sri Lanka Kotagala dips on profit-taking.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Kotagala Plantations Ltd fell 4.85 percent or 1.25 rupees to 24.50 on Monday, on profit-taking, brokers said.</p>
<p>&quot;There is a lot of profit to take since the share rose to 25.75 rupees last week,&quot; said a local broker.</p>
<p>Plantation shares have been the focus since tea and rubber prices are expected to be good in 1997, analysts said.</p>
<p>Kotagala Plantations is one of six privatised estate firms trading in Colombo.</p>
<p>--Colombo newsroom (941) 434319</p>
